WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Low-light cameras must trade among sensitivity, exposure time, noise, motion blur,

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.235
and detail.

00:00:06.235 --> 00:00:09.740
Increasing ISO or electronic gain can brighten an image while amplifying noise.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.280
A slower shutter can gather more light but blur moving subjects and aircraft motion.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.060
Automatic camera settings may produce an attractive preview that lacks reliable evidence.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.210
Dark areas can lose detail, highlights can clip, and color can shift.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:25.200
Review a sample and match settings to the mission rather than assuming brightness equals

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:25.780
quality.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.650
Thermal imaging can reveal heat differences under suitable conditions,

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.135
but it does not see through every material or identify cause by itself.

00:00:32.135 --> 00:00:34.900
Surface properties, distance, weather, calibration,

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.679
and time influence apparent temperature.

00:00:36.679 --> 00:00:40.960
Spotlights or illumination can improve a limited scene but may create glare, shadows,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.830
wildlife or community disturbance, privacy concerns, and additional power demand.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.460
Use only when lawful, necessary, and compatible with the mission and equipment.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.455
Match sensor capability to the question.

00:00:50.455 --> 00:00:54.100
If the mission requires detail the payload cannot capture reliably at night,

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.025
reschedule for daylight or use a different authorized method.

00:00:57.025 --> 00:01:00.660
Do not lower evidentiary standards because the flight was difficult.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.660
Report image limitations.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.940
Noise, blur, compression, low contrast, missing metadata,

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.531
and uncertain scale should remain visible in analysis.

00:01:07.531 --> 00:01:11.580
Poor imagery cannot support confident identity, intent, or condition judgments.
